","merged_at":"2024-10-28T06:48:10Z"},"body":"Fixes #98058\r\n\r\nThe main problem is that `vseparation` should be half above and half below when padding a menu item. Some of the current logic assumes that this value only works between menu items.\r\n\r\n- The first item is missing top padding\r\n    | Before | After|\r\n    |---|---|\r\n    | ![first before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/251336fb-5505-4e04-b27f-13b9b39c6598) | ![first after](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3aed344-3b22-41b2-8280-72e6b548b23a) |\r\n- When the menu needs scrolling, the last item is missing bottom padding\r\n    | Before | After|\r\n    |---|---|\r\n    | ![last before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1e62306-d006-4d97-8650-b195594efd2e) | ![last after](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55461dda-35c6-4ae2-a71d-0fa1807261a4) |\r\n- In addition, I found that menu's content margins are not taken into account when determining clickable area. This is noticeable when using exaggerated background margins.\r\n    | Before | After|\r\n    |---|---|\r\n    | ![margin before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3eaee118-fe01-454b-ae36-3a37ecc6f811) | ![margin after](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/96d3111a-60f5-4044-a775-2ad4291547c6) |\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url"